> On Mar 30, 2021, at 1:15 PM, John Klos <john@ziaspace.com> wrote:
>=20
> Hi,
>=20
> I've been running pbulk builds on my DS25 with no problems at all when =
the kernel is compiled without MULTIPROCESSOR. We have a full pbulk =
build of 2020Q4 :)
>=20
> I just tried with MULTIPROCESSOR with -current from 28-March-2021, but =
it paniced within a few hours of starting a pbulk scan.
>=20
> Does anyone have a clue about what might be going on here?

This indicates that the pmap is having TLB invalidations processed on =
the local CPU (id 0) and a remove CPU (id 1).  The local CPU is running =
at splhigh() (IPL 6 =3D=3D ALPHA_PSL_IPL_HIGH).  The local CPU has sent =
an IPI to the remote CPU to process the invalidation, and has timed out =
waiting for the remote CPU to process it.

Couple of things=E2=80=A6 I=E2=80=99m actually pretty surprised to see =
IPL =3D=3D 6 there.  At the top of pmap_tlb_shootnow() is the following:

        /*
         * Acquire the shootdown mutex.  This will also block IPL_VM
         * interrupts and disable preemption.  It is critically =
important
         * that IPIs not be blocked in this routine.
         */
        KASSERT((alpha_pal_rdps() & ALPHA_PSL_IPL_MASK) < =
ALPHA_PSL_IPL_CLOCK);
        mutex_spin_enter(&tlb_lock);

=E2=80=A6this is because on the Apha, IPIs come in at the same IPL as =
the clock interrupt, which is IPL =3D=3D 5.

tlb_lock is initialized thus:

        mutex_init(&tlb_lock, MUTEX_SPIN, IPL_VM);

..and IPL_VM is ALPHA_PSL_IPL_IO_HI, which is IPL =3D=3D 4.

So, something is raising our IPL to IPL_HIGH somewhere.  How rude!

mutex_spin_enter() is just an alias for mutex_vector_enter() on Alpha, =
so looking there, we see that MUTEX_SPIN_SPLRAISE() does:

        s =3D splraiseipl(MUTEX_SPIN_IPL(mtx));

=E2=80=A6and:

#define MUTEX_SPIN_IPL(mtx)             ((mtx)->mtx_ipl)

So, something is a little fishy here.  I think there=E2=80=99s a chance =
that there is some slight brokenness with spin mutexes on Alpha that =
only show up on MULTIPROCESSOR kernels.  I=E2=80=99ll take a deeper look =
a little later today.






